Margaret later needed $15,000 for emergency home repairs and was charged a $900 surrender fee. That fact is important because it shows the liquidity risk was not theoretical. For a retired senior with modest income and limited savings, emergency liquidity needs are foreseeable. A recommendation that exposed her to surrender penalties for accessing her own funds is inconsistent with preservation of capital and liquidity needs.

